    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Magic Potion\r\n\r\nUse `magical_potion_ingredients.csv` to practice filtering and aggregating data.\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 1]\r\nCreate a filtered DataFrame containing ingredients that:\r\n\r\n- Have a `Category` of `\"root\"`\r\n- Have a non-null `Source`\r\n\r\nUse AND (`&`) to combine the conditions. Print the first five rows.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 2]\r\nCreate a filtered DataFrame containing ingredients whose `Effect` ends with `\"ing\"`. Print the first five rows.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 3]\r\nCreate a filtered DataFrame containing ingredients that:\r\n\r\n- Have a `Rarity` of `\"legendary\"`\r\n- Have a `Source` of `\"forest\"`\r\n- Have an `Effect` of either `\"transformation\"` or `\"healing\"`\r\n\r\nUse parentheses to group the two Effect conditions. Print the first five rows.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 4]\r\nGroup the data by `Category`. Calculate the sum and median of `QuantityAvailable` for each category. Print the summary.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [Need Help?]\r\nUse AI Tutor to look up pandas documentation, explain your filter, or request a hint. When debugging a compound filter, check what each condition returns before combining the conditions.\r\n:::",
